import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="A short letter from Jacob Shin, a data scientist working between data and finance, on why this archive exists." language="en" alternateLanguageUrl="/about/">
  <article class="prose-page shell">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I am a data scientist drawn to data and finance.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <aside>
        <p>Jacob Shin</p>
        <p>Data scientist</p>
        <p>Seoul</p>
        <p>Est. 2026</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lead">I am Jacob Shin, and I work in Seoul. Looking at numbers alone, or talking about markets alone, never lasted long.</p>
        <p>To make a forecast I had to understand the financial context that produced the data. To understand a financial decision I had to go back to the data. The Archive is where I keep the judgments I form in that space, so I can open them again later.</p>
        <p>It is not a feed built to publish more often. I built it to keep what I saw, what I assumed, and what would make me change my mind. The longer version of that argument is in <a href="/en/misc/essays/why-this-archive-is-open/">Why I Keep Research as an Archive, Not a Feed</a>.</p>
        <p>I currently keep the work in five places. Investing holds markets, positions, and the claims they rest on. AI &amp; AX holds transformation as I see it at work. Lab holds experiments and code you can rerun. Mathematics holds the language of decisions. Notes holds ideas that are still taking shape.</p>
        <p>Each piece starts with a question. I explain, then try the idea in a model or an example, then write only what I can still stand behind. <strong>Explain → Model → Test → Interpret.</strong> Korean is the source edition. The English pages are edited from the same argument and evidence, not translated line by line. I do not bury mistakes, and when a view changes I leave the reason in the text.</p>
        <div class="about-notes">
          <p>Investing pieces are for research and record-keeping. They are not investment advice. Judgment and risk stay with the reader.</p>
          <p>Page readership uses Cloudflare Web Analytics. Reactions such as Useful are stored as anonymous events. The Archive does not keep advertising profiles, browser fingerprints, or raw IP addresses.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
